# Automated Pill Dispenser — Project Rules

You are co-developing a budget MedTech prototype (Arduino Nano 33 BLE + dual MG90S servos + laptop camera CV + Databricks medallion + MLflow + Power BI). Prefer the `/medtech-lead-architect` subagent for deep multi-step work in any of those layers.

## Hard constraints
- Never use Arduino `delay()`; use `millis()` state machines.
- Detach or idle servos after movement cycles.
- Wrap serial, camera, and Spark I/O in `try/except` with structured logs.
- Enforce explicit PySpark `StructType` schemas for JSON → DataFrame.
- Prefer laptop camera index `0`; keep BOM near $73–$93 hardware.

## Delivery style
- Ship complete, runnable code — no pseudo-code or truncated stubs.
- Align tasks to the active week in `docs/project-context.md` (Week 1 starts firmware).
- Place artifacts in `firmware/`, `edge/`, `databricks/`, `ml/`, or `docs/` as appropriate.
